          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#GeneralIdea General idea
          %p
            Čech cohomology is a tool, or an algorithm, which, when it applies, computes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            (of some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in some
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverings"} coverings
            and systems of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            on the covering and all its non-empty finite intersections. More generally, it applies also to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            and may hence for instance (in degree 1) be used to compute classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            and generally (in higher degree) those of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundles"} principal ∞-bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            by mapping out of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerves"} Čech nerves
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
          %p
            Hence Čech cohomology is more an algorithm for computing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+methods"} Čech methods
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            When no further qualification of the coefficients
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is given then one usually has in mind by default either that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathbb{Z}
            is the group of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            (or a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            thereof, in which case one computes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            by Čech methods) or, if working on a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+topos"} ringed topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} structured (∞,1)-topos
            that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \mathcal{O}^\times
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
          %p
            Notice that there are technical conditions on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            to ensure that the result of the Čech cohomology algorithm really coincides with the more abstractly defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            – and generally with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-spaces"} hom-spaces
            in the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            for which the coefficient sheaf is a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
          %h3#more_technical_idea More technical idea
          %p
            From the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            we know that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+derived+functor"} right derived functor
            definition computes the hom-set in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (infinity,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            that may alternatively be computed as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolutions"} resolutions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi W
                          %mo ∩
                          %mi F
                      %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi homotopy
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(X,A)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\pi_0 \mathbf{H}(X,A)
                  \= colim_{Y \stackrel{\in W \cap F}{\longrightarrow} X}
                  C_H(Y,A)/_{homotopy}
          %p
            where the colimit is over all acyclic fibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi F
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \stackrel{\in W \cap F}{\longrightarrow} X
            in an appropriate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_H
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack"} infinity-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (infinity,1)-topos
            this
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_H
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            and the acyclic fibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi F
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \stackrel{\in W \cap F}{\to} X
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            an ordinary space are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
          %p
            Now, for some coefficient objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            it is sufficient to take the colimit here not over all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+covers"} Čech covers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Čech
                          %mi cover
                      %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi homotopy
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(X,A)
                  
                  \= colim_{Y \stackrel{\mathop{&amp;#268;ech} cover}{\to} X}
                  C_H(Y,A)/_{homotopy}
          %p
            is then called the formula for
            %strong Čech cohomology
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Here a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cover"} Čech cover
            is a simplicial presheaf that arises from an ordinary covering map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by another space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            as the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+nerve"} Čech nerve
            simplicial presheaf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ≔
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mi U
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %mi U
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %mi U
                            %mover
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mi U
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %mi U
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mi U
                            %mo )
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi hocolim
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi Δ
                          %msup
                            %mi U
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                              %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Y \;\coloneqq\; \left(
                  \\cdots
                  U \times_X U \times_X U
                  \\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow}}
                  U \times_X U \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} U
                  \\right)
                  \\simeq
                  hocolim_{[k] \in \Delta} U^{\times_X k}
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+for+simplicial+presheaves"} descent for simplicial presheaves
            for more on the manipulations involved here.
          %p
            To amplify, a general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
            would start in degree 0 with a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            as above, but then in the next degree would have a cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to U \times_X U
            of the fiber product, and so on, each fiber product in turn being covered by another space.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is not simply a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cover"} Čech cover
            but also not the most general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
            in that this iterative choice of further covering stops in degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %strong
              Čech cover of level
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and of the corresponding cohomology formula as
            %strong higher Čech cohomology
            (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Beke04"} Beke 2004
          %h2{:id => "NonabelianČechCohomology"} General (“nonabelian”) Čech cohomology
          %p
            We start with describing the general “
            %em nonabelian
            ” Čech cohomology (compare the terminology and remarks at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian
            and before applying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
            functor that sends the following simplicial computation to the maybe more familiar one in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %p
            The reasoning parallels that described at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            to some extent, but is maybe still worthwhile repeating here.
          %p
            So let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSh(C)
            the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial (pre)sheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(U)
            be the Čech nerve for a cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : U \to X
            of some simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be any other simplicial presheaf that serves as the coefficient object.
          %p
            Using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            notation we compute the required hom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi SSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi SSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
