          %h2{:id => "AbelianČechCohomology"} Abelian Čech cohomology
          %p
            In much of the literature
            %em Čech cohomology
            denotes exclusively the abelian case, which we now describe.
          %p
            In the special case that the coefficient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is in the image of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo +
                  %mo →
                  %mi sAb
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N : Ch_+ \to sAb \to SSet
          %p
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            with values in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            that happen to be abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groups"} simplicial groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            by making use of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            that provides an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
            between simplicial sets with values in abelian groups and non-negatively graded chain complexes.
          %h3{:id => "AbelianČechCohomologyDefinition"} Definition
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            which gives the traditional definition of Čech cohomology with coefficients in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+abelian+groups"} sheaves of abelian groups
          %p Let
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                be a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mo •
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∂
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∂
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ∂
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet = (\cdots \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_2 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_1 \stackrel{\partial}{\to} A_0)
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (i.e. on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \colon Op(X)
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                with the usal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
                be an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p We write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi k
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %mi ⋯
                  %munder
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U_{i_0,\cdots i_k}
                  \\coloneqq
                  U_{i_0}
                  \\underset{X}{\times}
                  U_{i_1}
                  \\underset{X}{\times}
                  \\cdots
                  \\underset{X}{\times}
                  U_{i_k}
          %p
            for the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \to U_2
            and given any group element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A_\bullet(U_2)
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a|_{U_1}
            for its restriction along this map.
          %p
            More generally, we may allow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to be any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            (which in the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
            above.) Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            is a chain complex of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
            on that site.
          #CechComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Čech complex)
            %p
              The
              %strong Čech cochain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\bullet((X,\{U_i\}),A_\bullet)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with respect to the cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              and with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
              is in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi l
                            %mo ,
                            %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo =
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mi l
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^k((X,\{U_i\}),A_\bullet)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\oplus_{{l,n} \atop {k = n-l}}
                    \\oplus_{i_0, i_1, \cdots, i_n}
                    A_l(U_{i_0, \cdots, i_n})
            %p
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of the values of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
              on the given intersections as indicated; and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d
                    \\colon
                    C^{k}((X,\{U_i\}),A_\bullet)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    C^{k+1}((X,\{U_i\}),A_\bullet)
            %p
              is defined componentwise (see at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+calculus"} matrix calculus
              for conventions on maps between
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi k
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi A
                            %mi a
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi k
                            %mi δ
                            %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi k
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi k
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi k
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ≤
                                %mi j
                                %mo ≤
                                %mi k
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi j
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi j
                                    %mo −
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi j
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi k
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mn 0
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi ⋯
                                    %mo ,
                                    %msub
                                      %mi i
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi k
                                        %mo +
                                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (d a)_{i_0, \cdots, i_{k+1}}
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    (\partial_A a + (-1)^k \delta a)_{i_0, \cdots, i_{k+1}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\partial_A a_{i_0, \cdots, i_{k+1}}
                    +
                    (-1)^k
                    \\sum_{0 \leq j \leq k+1} (-1)^{j}
                    a_{i_0, \cdots, i_{j-1}, i_{j+1}, \cdots, i_{k+1}}
                    |_{U_{i_0, \cdots, i_{k+1}}}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              where on the right the sum is over all components of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              obtained via the canonical restrictions obtained by discarding one of the original
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k+1)
              subscripts.
            %p
              The
              %strong Čech cohomology
              groups of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with coefficients in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
              %strong relative to the given cover
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              groups of the Čech complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Cech
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_{Cech}^k((X,\{U_i\}), A_\bullet)
                    \\coloneqq
                    H^k(C^\bullet((X,\{U_i\}),A_\bullet))
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %strong Čech cohomology
              groups as such are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+limit"}> directed limit
              ”) of these groups over refinements of covers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Cech
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Cech
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^k_{Cech}(X, A_\bullet)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_{\{U_i \to X\}}
                    H_{Cech}^k((X,\{U_i\}), A_\bullet)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Often Čech cohomology is considered for the case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
