          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The following derivation of abelian Čech cohomology from nonabelian Čech cohomology restricted to nerves of chain complexes needs of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              only that it is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_recovering_abelian_ech_cohomology Proposition (recovering abelian Čech cohomology)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
              be a sheaf with values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_+
              and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(A_\bullet)
              for the corresponding simplicial sheaf under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              operation of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            %p
              Then the general (nonabelian) Čech cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(A_\bullet)
              as defined above coincides with the cohomology of the Čech complex of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi colim
                      %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
