            into all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact space
              the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˇ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\check{H}(X,A) \to H(X,A)
            %p
              from Čech cohomology to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              is an isomorphism from every
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi Ch
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Sh(X, Ch_+)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p Recalled as theorem 1.3.13 in
            %ul
              %li
                Brylinski,
                %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is not paracompact, we still have the following condition under which Čech cohomology computes
            = succeed "-." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a complex of sheaves, there is a canonical morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_0(C(U,A)_\bullet) \to H(X,A)
          %p
            from the cohomology of the Čech complex with respect to a cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+covers"} Čech covers
            into all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercovers"} hypercovers
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a complex of sheaves on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              concentrated in a single degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \geq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              such that the
              = succeed "-cohomology" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\forall U_{i_0 , \cdots, i_k} H(U_{i_0, \cdots, i_k},A) = 0
            %p Then the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_0(C(U,A)_\bullet) \to H(X,A)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p One considers the spectral sequence associated with the Čech double complex. Details are on page 28 of
            %ul
              %li
                Brylinski,
                %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
          %h3#examples Examples
          %p We now list examples for abelian Čech cohomology expressed in terms of the Čech complex described above.
          %h4#line_bundles Line bundles
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(1)
            be the circle group, an abelian group. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathbf{B}G)
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bar+construction"} bar construction
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U(1)[1]
                  \\,\coloneqq\, ( \cdots \to 0 \to U(1) \to 0 )
                  \\,.
          %p Equivalently we get the corresponding simplicial sheaves and complexes of sheaves, eg
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi W
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U(1)[1] : W \mapsto
                  ( \cdots \to 0 \to Hom(W,U(1)) \to 0 )
                  \\,.
          %p
            So given a cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            a Čech cocycle is a collection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c = ( \{g_{i j} \in U(1)[1](U_{i j})\}|_{i,j})
          %p such that the Čech differential evaluated on it
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mrow
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi U
                              %mo ,
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi c
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                              %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                                  %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi k
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                                  %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi j
                                  %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  (d_{C(U,U(1)[1])} c)_{i j k}
                  \&amp;=
                  g_{j k}|_{U_{i j k}} - g_{i k}|_{U_{i j k}}
                  + g_{i j}|_{U_{i j k}} )
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p vanishes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{i j}|_{U_{i j k}} + g_{j k}|_{U_{i j k}} = g_{i k}|_{U_{i j k}}
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j, k
          %p
            Here now we write plus signs for the operation in the abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            which above we have written by juxtaposition or using a dot. So up to notation for the group operation this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{i j} g_{j k} = g_{i k}
          %p
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{i j k}
            as before in the nonabelian case of Čech cocycles for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
          %p
            Here and from now on we shall notationally suppress the restriction maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)|_{U_{i_0, i_1, \cdots, i_n}}
            as they are unambiguously obviuous in every case.
          %h4#line_bundle_gerbes Line bundle gerbes
          %p
            Similarly by shifting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            ever higher in chain degree, one finds Čech cocycles for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
          %p A Čech cocycle for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U(1)[2]
                  \\,\coloneqq\, ( \cdots \to 0 \to U(1) \to 0 \to 0 )
                  \\,.
          %p is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c = ( \{g_{i j k} \in U(1)[2](U_{i j k})\}|_{i,j, k})
          %p
            such that on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{i,j,k,l}
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi l
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                      %mi l
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                      %mi l
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{i j k} - g_{i j l} + g_{i k l} - g_{j k l} = 0
          %p which in the nonabelian context would be written as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                      %mi l
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                      %mi l
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                      %mi l
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{i j k} g_{i k l} = g_{i j l} g_{j k l}
                  \\,.
          %h4#echdeligne_cohomology Čech-Deligne cohomology
          %p
            When refining the complexes of sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)[n]
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+cohomology"} Deligne complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi D
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U(1)[n] \hookrightarrow \mathbb{Z}(n+1)_D^\infty
          %p and then evaluating Čech cohomology with coefficients in the Deligne complex, we obtain the formulas for Čech-Deligne cohomology.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
                a cocycle is a collection
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      ( A_i \in \Omega^1(U_i),
                      g_{i j} \in C^\infty(U_{i j}, U(1)) )
              %p
                such that for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi log
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi j
                      %mo −
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      d log g_{i j} + A_i - A_j -  = 0
              %p
                and for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j ,k
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      g_{i j} g_{j k} = g_{i k}
                      \\,.
              %p
                Such cocycles classify
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
                with
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
              %p
                These
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
                Čech-Deligne cocycles appear naturally in the study of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
                a cocycle is a collection
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      ( B_i \in \Omega^2(U_i),
                      A_{i j} \in \Omega^1(U_{i j}),
                      g_{i j k} \in C^\infty(U_{i j k}, U(1)) )
              %p
                such that for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      d A_{i j} + B_i - B_j = 0
              %p
                and for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i,j ,k
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mi d
                      %mi log
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A_{i j} - A_{i k} + A_{j k} + d log g_{i j k} = 0
              %p
                and for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi l
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j, k ,l
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi k
                          %mi l
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                          %mi l
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mi k
                          %mi l
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      g_{i j k} g_{i k l} = g_{i j l} g_{j k l}
                      \\,.
              %p
                Such cocycles classify
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
                with connection.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              For discussion of the isomorphism between isomorphism classes of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
              and Čech cohomology on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              with coefficients in continuous functions with values in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "topological+vector+bundle#TransitionFunctionsAndCechCohomology"} there
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Classical accounts (in the generality of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"}> Alexander Grothendieck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A General Theory of Fibre Spaces With Structure Sheaf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~leila.schneps/grothendieckcircle/Kansasnotes.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Grothendieck-FibreSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Frenkel"}> Jean Frenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomologie à valeurs dans un faisceau non abélien
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Frenkel"}> Jean Frenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomologie non abélienne et espaces fibrés
                %strong 85
                (1957) 135-220 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/BSMF_1957__85__135_0"}> numdam:BSMF_1957__85__135_0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Godement58
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roger+Godement"}> Roger Godement
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topologie algébrique et theorie des faisceaux
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1252
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.editions-hermann.fr/livre/topologie-algebrique-et-theorie-des-faisceaux-roger-godement"} webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Godement-TopologieAlgebrique.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Historical survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Edwards"}> David Edwards
              , Harold M. Hastings:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Čech Theory: Its past, present, and future
              %strong 10
              3 (1980) 429-468 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.rmjm/1250128825"}> euclid:rmjm/1250128825
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Torsten+Wedhorn"}> Torsten Wedhorn
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Torsors and Non-abelian Čech Cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em Manifolds, Sheaves, and Cohomology
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-658-10633-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-658-10633-1
          %p
            Exposition in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
          %ul
            %li#Alvarez85
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Orlando+Alvarez"}> Orlando Alvarez
              , Section 4 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological quantization and cohomology
              %strong 100
              2 (1985) 279-309 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01212452"}> doi:10.1007/BF01212452
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103943448"} euclid:cmp/1103943448
          %p
            and via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+geometry"} complex analytic geometry
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Weiss"}> Michael Weiss
              \:
              %em The Search for a Global Primitive – Cech Cohomology with Coefficients in a Sheaf
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Weiss-CechCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A discussion of Čech cohomology in the wider context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            particularly realized in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            and with an emphasis on the shades of notions between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cover"} Čech cover
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
            is
          %ul
            %li#Beke04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tibor+Beke"}> Tibor Beke
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher Čech theory
              %strong 32
              4 (2004) 293–322 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10977-004-0840-0"}> doi:10.1007/s10977-004-0840-0
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://faculty.uml.edu/tbeke/cech.pdf"} pdf
          %p Abelian Čech cohomology is discussed in some detail in section I.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              %em Loop spaces, characteristic classes and geometric quantization
          %p
            A discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            with an eye towards the distinction between Čech and hyperlocalization is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              %em Sheaves and Homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.uoregon.edu/~ddugger/cech.html"}> web
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/cech.pdf"} pdf
          %p (But beware that, while providing useful insights, these are unfinished abandoned notes that seem to have some gaps right at this point.)
          %p
            A long list of reasons why higher Čech cohomology might is after all better behaved than its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercompletion"} hypercompletion
            where a cycle is with respect to an arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
            is in section 6.5.4,
            %strong Descent versus Hyperdescent
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p The relation between smooth and continuous Čech cohomology is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              Christoph Müller,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Wockel"} Christoph Wockel
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivalences of smooth and continuous principal bundles with infinite-dimensional structure groups
